{"id":"rs_tmp_0ejmz0uhun34","type":"reasoning","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"reasoning_text","text":"I'm weighing where this config concept should live: omp's own config.yml is only written to when omp itself reads those keys, whereas a knowledge home is purely omp-ui's notion that omp wouldn't need to consume. I'm checking precedent — ADR-0047 moved reviewRoster out of REVIEW.yml into ProjectRecord, while ADR-0005 went the other direction, removing ProjectRecord.advisor once omp config could express it, which is the opposite situation here.

I'm also unsure whether omp validates or warns on unknown config keys, and noting that .omp/ is typically gitignored and shared across worktree checkouts, so committing a machine-specific vault path there would be wrong regardless. I want to check CONTEXT.md around line 274 and ADR-0047 directly, and grep for "knowledge" to see if this terminology already exists somewhere.

"}],"summary":[],"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ","format":"anthropic-claude-v1"}

{"id":"rs_tmp_un1b08i91oq","type":"reasoning","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"reasoning_text","text":"I'm noting that omp settings belong in .omp/config.yml while omp-ui-only state lives in ProjectRecord, per the ADR-0047 precedent. The knowledge home — which Obsidian vault/folder backs a project — is consumed only by omp-ui, not omp itself, and since the vault path is machine-specific and absolute to a user's home directory, it shouldn't live in a shared git config.

I'm settling on ProjectRecord as the right place for this, and since picking is effectively a decision, I'll go ahead and write a short note documenting it as instructed.

